      "date": "2026-11-20 01:38:35.000000000",
      "message": "Patch Set 6:\n\n(2 comments)\n\nAI code review results below, please doublecheck\n\nLooks good. I simulated the new remote wait script through the do_nodes() quoting and found no functional problems: escaped regex states like \\(FULL\\|IDLE\\), the DISCONN early exits, timeout failure, the no-mount skip, and the set_hostid() byte order all behave like the rpc.sh versions. Two optional nits inline for the next refresh; no need to re-spin for them.",
