        "subject": "LU-20076 tests: wait for imports without rpc.sh",
        "message": "LU-20076 tests: wait for imports without rpc.sh\n\nAfter a target starts, conf-sanity and fail() wait for the clients'\nimports to reconnect through rpc.sh, as do the OSC, MGC and OSP\nimport waits on the servers. Each rpc.sh call sources the test\nframework and its config on the remote node, only to run a loop of\n\"lctl get_param\" checks. CI's conf-sanity logs show about 1,455\nrpc.sh calls per run at about 2.4 s each, most of them these waits\nand set_hostid.\n\nSend each wait as one remote script instead. It checks the same\nimports for the same states with the same timeout, skips a node\nwith no client mounted as before, and prints the same messages and\ndebug log marks. With VERBOSE, the debug log mark for the command\nis made by the same remote command, not a second one. set_hostid\nis a plain remote command too.\n\nThis sits on LU-20076 tests: ping MDC/OSC imports to revalidate,\nwhich it needs. A client wait that returns at once can accept an\nimport that is FULL but was already evicted, and without rpc.sh\nstartup in front of it sanity-quota test_91 hit that in CI. The\nping that change adds before the wait is sent the same way.\n\nWith fail() back sooner, sanity test_17o set its fail_loc while a\nquota slave's reintegration was still connecting to the master. The\nfailed enqueue leaks a lock reference and a later MDT umount hangs,\nso the test now waits for reintegration to finish first.\n\nMeasured on a 2-node cluster (one server with 4 MDTs and 4 OSTs,\none client, about 0.19 s per ssh), VERBOSE, mean of 10 calls:\n\n                            cmds      master   patched\n  client wait, 2 nodes     2 -> 1     0.53 s    0.21 s\n  MDT OSC wait, 4 MDTs    16 -> 12    3.67 s    2.28 s\n  MGC wait                 4 -> 3     0.90 s    0.56 s\n  set_hostid               2 -> 1     0.51 s    0.20 s\n\nThe remaining commands of the OSC and MGC waits read at_min. rpc.sh\ncosts only 0.13 s to start there, since that cluster's config names\nthe MGS NID. conf-sanity 0 1 2 3 5a 17 41a 50a 140 162 pass as on\nmaster, with rpc.sh calls down from 99 to 18, which load and unload\nmodules.\n\nIn CI, where an rpc.sh call costs about 2.3 s against 0.35 s for a\nplain remote command, each wait saves about 2 s. Counting the 2,000\nclient import waits CI logs per conf-sanity run as about 1,000\ncalls on 2 clients each, plus 260 server import waits and 115\nset_hostid calls, that is about 45 minutes of a 9.4 hour run.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=conf-sanity,replay-single\nTest-Parameters: trivial fstype=zfs testlist=conf-sanity\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=recovery-small,sanity-quota\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-sonnet-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: Id1c5fc83fceca3464776f653caf1916c1b2a8170\n"
      },
